From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH EXPERIMENTAL] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: add system_pd with deepest system idle state

*** EXPERIMENTAL — sm8550-systempd-exp branch only. Do NOT merge to main
    without on-device validation (armada#274). ***

SM8550 devices never enter AOSD/CXSD during s2idle (qcom_stats shows
aosd=cxsd=0 on every board tested: Odin 2, Thor, RP6). Unlike SM8750,
X1E80100 and Kaanapali, the SM8550 dtsi describes no system-level power
domain: apps_rsc votes on cluster_pd, so RPMh resource votes are only
coordinated down to the cluster level and the AOP never sees a full
system idle.

This ports the upstream SM8750 pattern verbatim
(arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi lines 208-214, 319-331, 5743):

 - add a domain_ss3 system idle state under domain-idle-states;
 - insert system_pd (power-domain-system) above cluster_pd and rewire
   cluster_pd -> system_pd;
 - move the apps_rsc power-domains vote from cluster_pd to system_pd.

The psci-suspend-param for domain_ss3 is UNVERIFIED on SM8550 silicon.
SM8750 uses 0x0200c354 (same param as X1E80100 domain_ss3). No SM8550
downstream (Xiaomi/OnePlus/QCOM) ships a PL2-level system state — all
stop at APSS_OFF (cluster). Candidate params if 0x0200c354 is rejected
by the SM8550 AOP/TZ: 0x0200c344, 0x4200c344.

On-device validation checklist (Odin 2):
 1. Boot: no new psci/printk errors, cpuidle domains registered
    (dmesg "psci: OSI mode supported" already present);
 2. s2idle soak: /sys/kernel/debug/qcom_stats aosd/cxsd counters
    increment (structurally zero before this patch);
 3. Resume: clean (no hang/hard reset — the PCIe suspend-OPP floor
    from 0513+0520 is a prerequisite, keep them BEFORE this patch);
 4. Battery soak ~60-100 mA expected vs 128-170 mA measured stock.

If AOP rejects the param, the fallback ladder is one-line param swaps
recorded above; if the SoC hangs at freeze entry, drop this patch
entirely (revert is clean: pure DT addition, no driver dependency).

Depends-on: 0513 (PCI: honour opp suspend_opp), 0520 (pcie suspend opp
DT) — without them, wake from a DDR/LLCC-off state hard-resets.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
index 3962019..b9fa02d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -382,6 +382,14 @@
 				exit-latency-us = <4400>;
 				min-residency-us = <10150>;
 			};
+
+			domain_ss3: domain-sleep-0 {
+				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x0200c354>;
+				entry-latency-us = <2800>;
+				exit-latency-us = <4400>;
+				min-residency-us = <10150>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -829,6 +837,12 @@
 		cluster_pd: power-domain-cluster {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_sleep_0>, <&cluster_sleep_1>;
+			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
+		};
+
+		system_pd: power-domain-system {
+			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+			domain-idle-states = <&domain_ss3>;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -5759,7 +5773,7 @@
 			qcom,drv-id = <2>;
 			qcom,tcs-config = <ACTIVE_TCS    3>, <SLEEP_TCS     2>,
 					  <WAKE_TCS      2>, <CONTROL_TCS   0>;
-			power-domains = <&cluster_pd>;
+			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
 
 			apps_bcm_voter: bcm-voter {
 				compatible = "qcom,bcm-voter";
